// Mailbox block-level verification plan (vPlan), for DVPlan.
//
// Status: skeleton. Section structure, metric names and requirement references are in place; the
// evidence is not.
//
// What this file is
// -----------------
// The vPlan holds the features to verify and, once filled, the evidence that each one is covered.
// The testplan (mailbox_testplan.hjson) holds the testpoints, meaning the tests that produce that
// evidence. Where a feature needs a test, the test is in the testplan and reaches this plan as a
// testcase item, so the two files are not copies of each other.
//
// Structure
// ---------
// Sections group features by where a feature is measured:
//
//   interfaces          The two AXI4-Lite ports, the two interrupt outputs, clock and reset.
//   functional_features Behaviour observed from the ports, split into the legal behaviour and the
//                       exception handling.
//   structural_features Behaviour measured inside the design.
//   scenarios           End-to-end use cases.
//
// Requirement references
// ----------------------
// Each metric cites the requirement it verifies in Reference, one `<document>#<section>` token per
// line. The token carries no spaces, so dvplan trace never reads a word of it as a spec tag.
// The documents are:
//
//   axi_lite_mailbox  hw/vendor/pulp_axi/doc/axi_lite_mailbox.md, the block specification
//   mocha_mailbox     doc/proj/mailbox.md, the Mocha instance and its parameters
//   stages            doc/proj/stages.md, the verification stages
//
// The block specification is vendored, so it cannot carry spec tags without a vendor patch.
//
// Open specification questions
// ----------------------------
// Where the documents do not settle the expected result, the Description ends with a TODO stating
// the open question, and Issue names the issue tracking it once there is one. Such a metric stays a
// coverage hole until the question is decided. The behaviour of the current RTL is not an expected
// result, so a test that passes against it earns no coverage here.
//
// What is deliberately absent
// ---------------------------
// Items, Metric_Type, Owner and Weight come once the environment exists and it is known which
// covergroup, assertion, test or inspection answers for each feature. Goal is set only where
// stages.md names a figure.
//
// Milestone is set on metric leaves, because a milestone on a section applies to everything below
// it. Priority 0 marks an open specification question that has to be settled before the tests
// around it can be written. Everything else is 1.
{
    mailbox:
    {
        Reference:
            '''
            axi_lite_mailbox#axi4-lite-mailbox
            mocha_mailbox#mailbox
            '''
        Description: Two AXI4-Lite subordinate ports connected back to back over a pair of FIFOs, with a per-port interrupt on fill level and on error. Verified as instantiated in Mocha, with AxiDataWidth 64, MailboxDepth 3 and level-sensitive active-high interrupts.
        Node_Type: dut_name

        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        // Interfaces                                                        //
        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        interfaces:
        {
            Description: Protocol compliance and signal-level behaviour at the ports of axi_lite_mailbox. What the ports carry functionally lives under functional_features.
            Node_Type: section_title

            axil_ports:
            {
                Description: The two AXI4-Lite subordinate ports.
                Node_Type: section_title

                axil_write_handshake:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#module-ports
                    Description: Each port completes every write whichever of AW and W arrives first, under random valid and ready timing on the AW, W and B channels.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                axil_read_handshake:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#module-ports
                    Description: Each port completes every read under random valid and ready timing on the AR and R channels.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                axil_protocol:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#module-ports
                    Description: Every response is OKAY or SLVERR, and the B and R payloads hold steady while their valid is high and ready is low.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                port_base_address:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                        mocha_mailbox#mailbox
                        '''
                    Description: Each port decodes the register set from its own base_addr_i, 0x2001_0000 for the main port and 0x1000 for the external port in Mocha.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V1
                    Priority: 1
                }
            }
            irq:
            {
                Description: The two interrupt outputs, irq_o[0] for the main port and irq_o[1] for the external port.
                Node_Type: section_title

                irq_level:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#module-parameters
                        axi_lite_mailbox#irqp-register
                        '''
                    Description: Each interrupt output is high exactly while the IRQP register of its port is non-zero, with IrqEdgeTrig 0 and IrqActHigh 1 as instantiated in Mocha.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
            }
            clk_rst:
            {
                Description: Clock and reset.
                Node_Type: section_title

                reset_values:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                        axi_lite_mailbox#status-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#error-register
                        '''
                    Description: Out of reset STATUS reads 0x1, with only EMPTY set, and every other readable register reads 0. TODO: the register table gives ERROR a default of 0x0 while the ERROR bit table gives READ_ERR a reset value of 1.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V1
                    Priority: 0
                }
            }
        }

        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        // Functional features                                               //
        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        functional_features:
        {
            Description: Behaviour observed from the two ports.
            Node_Type: section_title

            legal_behaviour:
            {
                Description: What the mailbox does for accesses its specification allows.
                Node_Type: section_title

                data_transfer:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#mboxw-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#mboxr-register
                        '''
                    Description: A 64-bit word written to MBOXW on one port is read unchanged from MBOXR on the other port, in write order, in both directions.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V1
                    Priority: 1
                }
                fifo_depth:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#module-parameters
                        mocha_mailbox#mailbox
                        '''
                    Description: Each direction holds exactly MailboxDepth words, 3 in Mocha, before it reports full.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                status_empty_full:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#status-register
                    Description: STATUS.EMPTY is set exactly while the port's read FIFO is empty, and STATUS.FULL exactly while its write FIFO is full.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                status_threshold_flags:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#status-register
                    Description: STATUS.WFIFOL is set exactly while the write FIFO level is higher than WIRQT, and STATUS.RFIFOL exactly while the read FIFO level is higher than RIRQT. TODO: the RFIFOL description reads "Write FIFO level is less or equal to the threshold" for 0; the read FIFO is assumed.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                register_map:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                    Description: The ten registers sit at base_addr_i + n * AxiDataWidth/8, 8-byte steps in Mocha, with the access type the specification gives each. TODO: the register table lists CTRL as R/W while its bit table lists both bits as W.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V1
                    Priority: 0
                }
                threshold_registers:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#wirqt-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#rirqt-register
                        '''
                    Description: WIRQT and RIRQT each hold a $clog2(MailboxDepth)-bit threshold, 2 bits in Mocha, and a written value larger than or equal to MailboxDepth reads back as MailboxDepth - 1.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                threshold_irq_status:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#irqs-register
                    Description: IRQS.WTIRQ and IRQS.RTIRQ are set when the write or read FIFO level rises above its threshold, stay set, and clear only when 1 is written to them. TODO: the specification calls the bits sticky and set "when the trigger condition is fulfilled", without saying whether a bit acknowledged while the level is still above the threshold is set again.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 0
                }
                error_irq_status:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#irqs-register
                    Description: IRQS.EIRQ is set by a read from an empty mailbox or a write to a full one, stays set, and clears only when 1 is written to it.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                irq_status_without_enable:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#irqs-register
                    Description: IRQS bits are set whether or not the matching IRQEN bit is set.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                irq_enable_pending:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#irqen-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#irqp-register
                        '''
                    Description: IRQP equals IRQS AND IRQEN bit for bit, and the port's interrupt is the OR of its IRQP bits.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                flush:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#ctrl-register
                    Description: Writing 1 to CTRL bit 0 empties the port's write FIFO and to bit 1 its read FIFO, a FIFO is flushed when either port asks for it, and the register returns to 0 after the write. TODO: the specification names the two CTRL bits WTIRQ and RTIRQ, like the interrupt bits; flush write FIFO and flush read FIFO are assumed.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
            }
            exception_handling:
            {
                Description: What the mailbox does for accesses its specification refuses or leaves open.
                Node_Type: section_title

                write_full:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#mboxw-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#error-register
                        '''
                    Description: A write to MBOXW while the write FIFO is full answers SLVERR, is never delivered, and sets ERROR.WRITE_ERR.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                read_empty:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#mboxr-register
                        axi_lite_mailbox#error-register
                        '''
                    Description: A read of MBOXR while the read FIFO is empty answers SLVERR and sets ERROR.READ_ERR.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                error_clear_on_read:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#error-register
                    Description: Reading ERROR returns the flags raised since it was last read and clears them. TODO: the specification does not say what happens to an error raised in the same cycle as ERROR is read.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 1
                }
                access_type_errors:
                {
                    Reference:
                        '''
                        axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                        axi_lite_mailbox#error-register
                        '''
                    Description: A write to an R register and a read of a W register answer SLVERR and change no state. TODO: the specification does not say whether such an access sets ERROR or IRQS.EIRQ, since ERROR only describes full and empty.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 0
                }
                unmapped_access:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                    Description: An access to an address that maps to no register changes no state. TODO: the specification does not give the response.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 0
                }
                partial_writes:
                {
                    Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#register-address-mapping
                    Description: A write with only some byte strobes set. TODO: the specification does not say what a partial write delivers through MBOXW or leaves in the R/W registers.
                    Node_Type: metric
                    Milestone: V2
                    Priority: 0
                }
            }
        }

        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        // Structural features                                               //
        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        structural_features:
        {
            Description: Behaviour measured inside axi_lite_mailbox.
            Node_Type: section_title

            code_coverage:
            {
                Reference: stages#hardware-ip-block-verification-stages
                Description: Line, branch, condition, toggle and FSM coverage of axi_lite_mailbox and the FIFOs it instantiates.
                Node_Type: metric
                Milestone: V2
                Priority: 1
                Goal: 90
            }
        }

        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        // Scenarios                                                         //
        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
        scenarios:
        {
            Description: End-to-end use cases.
            Node_Type: section_title

            request_response:
            {
                Reference:
                    '''
                    axi_lite_mailbox#axi4-lite-mailbox
                    mocha_mailbox#mailbox
                    '''
                Description: One port sends a request of several words, the other collects it on its read threshold interrupt and answers, and the first collects the answer on its own interrupt.
                Node_Type: metric
                Milestone: V2
                Priority: 1
            }
            concurrent_bidirectional:
            {
                Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#axi4-lite-mailbox
                Description: Both ports write and read at the same time, each FIFO filling and draining independently of the other.
                Node_Type: metric
                Milestone: V2
                Priority: 1
            }
            flush_during_traffic:
            {
                Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#ctrl-register
                Description: A flush from either port while words are in flight leaves both ports consistent, and the next word is delivered intact.
                Node_Type: metric
                Milestone: V2
                Priority: 1
            }
            reset_during_traffic:
            {
                Reference: axi_lite_mailbox#module-ports
                Description: A reset in the middle of traffic returns every register to its reset value, and the next word is delivered intact.
                Node_Type: metric
                Milestone: V2
                Priority: 1
            }
        }
    }
}
